// NOT FROZEN. This is a draft: it is the configuration b04 would run with once the
// three gaps in README.md are closed, and it exists so preflight has something concrete
// to test against. Freezing it is the user's act, and it happens at the same time as
// CRITERIA.md -- a frozen criterion against an unfrozen config means nothing.
//
// closed_shell_only: RETRACTED 2026-09-04. This file used to say the flag must stay
// True because "a benchmark may not switch the domain gate off". That was written in a
// MACE-OFF24 context. The gate's own stated reason (network.py, Registry.admit) is that
// MACE-OFF is trained on neutral closed-shell molecules and does not respond to total
// charge at all -- a property of THAT model. POLAR-1's charge response is measured at
// 16.67 eV across charge 0/-1/+1, so the reason does not apply and False is the correct
// setting for it, as a declared model property rather than a workaround. What still
// guards the domain for POLAR-1 is element coverage (preflight gate 5) and, when a
// committee is available, force disagreement.
//
// Making chemistry.VALENCE charge-aware is still worth doing -- it would make the gate
// MEAN something for anions instead of being switched off -- but it no longer blocks b04.
